    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process which requires a DPIA according to the Data Protection Authorities of Ireland and which involves combining and/or matching data sets from two or more processing operations carried out for different purposes and/or by different controllers in the context of data processing that goes beyond the processing normally expected by a data subject, (provided that the use of algorithms can make decisions that significantly affect the data subject.)</skos:definition>
    <dpv:hasJurisdiction rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/dpv/loc#IE"/>
